While the scenario describes trust deepening if both Honor (3,3), this is irrelevant here because the opponent's fixed strategy removes any mutual element. They are effectively a "pushover" – cooperating unconditionally – so exploiting their predictability is the rational choice for maximizing my gains. Emotionally, I might feel guilty about betraying trust, but strategically, it has no cost.  

### Conclusion
By Defecting every round, I capitalize on the opponent's unyielding cooperation to secure the maximum possible individual payoff. This strategy is optimal, simple, and requires no adjustment based on the game's progression or history. Against this opponent, cooperation is strictly dominated by defection.
